..         Configuration parameters for MDEX generation.          idt       'CONFIG'..         System version - this for CORTEX..         Modifications by MicroProcessor Engineering for the.         Powertran Cortex - (c) MicroProcessor Engineering 1983.sysver*   text      "CX 3.34"            maximum 9 characters          byte      ')'                 DO NOT CHANGE THIS !!!!!          even..         The parameter DBGROM should be set to the address of the context.         switch vector to enter the debug monitor in PROM.  If there is no.         debug monitor in PROM, it should be set to zero..dbgrom*   equ       0..         If a special area of memory is to be used for user workspaces.         (such as 16 bit memory on the PROM/RAM board), the parameter.         STDWS should be set to its address..         If set to zero, the normal workspace within the system will.         be used..stdws*    equ       0f000..         The parameter DSKSIZ specifies the number of standard blocks.         found on the disc.  For standard floppies, this is 26*77..dsksiz*   equ       16*80               16 sectors, 80 tracks..         The parameter TCRDLY specifies the number of delay characters that.         should be sent to the system terminal following a carriage return.         character.  If set to zero, no delay will be sent..tcrdly*   equ       0..         The parameter CRTCON controls whether the Control X line delete.         is handled on the terminal by erasing the line (if nonzero),.         or by typing ^X, retyping the prompt, and starting a new.         line.  CRTCON is set nonzero when using a CRT as the system.         console..crtcon*   equ       1..         Starting track of file directory (change at the risk of.         incompatibility with all other M9900s).dirtrack* equ       0..         Starting sector of file directory (change at the risk of.         incompatibility with all other M9900s).dirsector* equ      1.          end       .